  <h1 style="margin-top:1.1rem; margin-bottom:1.2rem;">Irene Iodice</h1>

  <img src="{{ base }}/images/bio.jpeg"
       alt="Photograph of Irene Iodice"
       style="float:left; width:33%; margin:0 30px 10px 0;">

  <p style="text-align:left;">
    I am an Assistant Professor of Economics at
    <strong>City St George's, University of London</strong>
    and a CESifo Research Network Affiliate. My research lies at the
    intersection of international trade and industrial organisation,
    with a focus on how trade policy, regulations, and technical standards
    shape firms' sourcing decisions, production networks, and responses
    to globalisation.
  </p>

  <div style="clear:both; margin-top:0.75rem;"></div>

  <p style="text-align:left;">
    My current work studies trade agreements and rules of origin,
    non-tariff measures and technical standards, and how international
    policy coordination shapes global production and trade.
  </p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:1.4rem; margin-bottom:0.8rem;">Research Interests</h2>
  <ul style="margin-top:0; line-height:1.45;">
    <li>Trade agreements, rules of origin, and global value chains</li>
    <li>Technical standards, non-tariff measures, and production networks</li>
    <li>International policy coordination and trade liberalisation</li>
    <li>Firm adjustment to trade and competitiveness shocks</li>
  </ul>

